

# Shared Basket - Project Specification

## Project Overview

Shared Basket is a collaborative web application that enables groups of users to manage shared shopping lists efficiently.

Each shopping group has its own workspace where members can collaborate by adding products, tracking purchases, managing expenses, and viewing shopping statistics. The application also analyzes historical shopping data to provide recommendations and future cost estimations.

The project must be implemented using a clean layered architecture and follow Java enterprise best practices.

---

# Required Technology Stack (Mandatory)

The following technologies **must** be used:

### Backend

* Java
* Spring Boot
* Spring MVC
* Spring Data JPA
* Hibernate
* Spring Security
* RESTful API

### Frontend

* JSF (JavaServer Faces)
* HTML
* CSS
* JavaScript

### Database

* PostgreSQL

No alternative frameworks should be substituted.

---

# Core Functional Requirements

## 1. Authentication

The system must support:

* User registration
* Login using email and password
* Secure password hashing
* Authentication using Spring Security
* User profile management

---

## 2. Shopping Groups

Users must be able to:

* Create shopping groups
* Generate invitation codes
* Join groups using invitation codes
* Request access to private groups
* Leave groups

Each shopping group maintains an independent shopping list and history.

---

## 3. Roles and Permissions

Each group contains two roles.

### Admin

Responsibilities:

* Manage group members
* Accept or reject join requests
* Remove members
* Manage group settings

### Member

Permissions:

* View shopping list
* Add products
* Edit products
* Mark products as purchased
* View statistics

Authorization must be enforced both in the backend and frontend.

---

## 4. Shopping List Management

Each shopping item contains:

* Product name
* Quantity
* Category
* Current price
* Status
* Creator
* Creation timestamp

Supported operations:

* Create item
* Update item
* Delete item
* Mark as purchased
* Change quantity
* Update price

---

## 5. Categories

Products belong to reusable categories.

Examples:

* Dairy
* Fruits
* Vegetables
* Drinks
* Bakery
* Cleaning Supplies

Categories should be managed independently from products.

---

## 6. Expense Tracking

The system must provide dashboards and reports including:

* Total spending
* Spending by category
* Spending by product
* Budget versus actual spending
* Purchase history
* Monthly and historical statistics

All analytics must be generated from stored shopping data.

---

## 7. Recommendations

The recommendation engine is a mandatory feature.

Using purchase history, the system should:

* Recommend frequently purchased products
* Suggest products previously bought by the group
* Estimate the expected cost of the current shopping basket
* Assist users in quickly rebuilding recurring shopping lists

---

## 8. Purchase History

Every completed purchase must be stored.

Each record includes:

* Product name
* Purchase price
* Purchase date
* Shopping group

Historical data serves both reporting and recommendation features.

---

## 9. Real-Time Synchronization

Real-time collaboration is a mandatory requirement.

Multiple users may edit the same shopping list simultaneously.

The system must:

* Synchronize updates in real time.
* Prevent conflicting concurrent updates.
* Prevent lost updates caused by simultaneous modifications.
* Ensure data consistency across all connected clients.

The architecture should support real-time communication (for example using WebSockets) together with appropriate concurrency control mechanisms.

---

# Database Model

The application should contain at least the following entities.

---

## User

Stores user information.

Fields:

* id
* fullName
* email
* passwordHash

---

## Group

Represents a shopping group.

Fields:

* id
* name
* description
* invitationCode
* createdBy
* createdAt

---

## GroupMember

Represents membership and permissions.

Fields:

* id
* groupId
* userId
* role
* joinedAt

---

## Category

Stores reusable product categories.

Fields:

* id
* name

---

## ShoppingItem

Represents a product in the shopping list.

Fields:

* id
* groupId
* categoryId
* productName
* quantity
* actualPrice
* status
* createdBy

---

## JoinRequest

Stores pending membership requests.

Fields:

* id
* groupId
* userId
* status
* createdAt

---

## PriceHistory

Stores historical purchases.

Fields:

* id
* productName
* price
* purchaseDate
* groupId

---

# Entity Relationships

* One User can belong to multiple Groups.
* One Group contains multiple Members.
* One Group contains multiple Shopping Items.
* One Shopping Item belongs to one Category.
* One Group contains multiple Join Requests.
* One Group contains multiple Price History records.

---

# REST API

The backend must expose RESTful endpoints for:

* Authentication
* User management
* Group management
* Join requests
* Member management
* Shopping items
* Categories
* Statistics
* Recommendations
* Purchase history

The JSF frontend must communicate with the backend exclusively through these REST APIs.

---

# Recommended Layered Architecture

```
Presentation Layer (JSF)

↓

REST Controllers

↓

Service Layer

↓

Repository Layer (Spring Data JPA)

↓

Hibernate ORM

↓

PostgreSQL
```

The business logic must reside exclusively in the Service layer.

Controllers should only validate requests and delegate operations.

Repositories should contain only persistence logic.

